    "intro_html":  "Sausage and peppers is street fair food, the smell that pulls you across a parking lot in July. Usually it lands on a hoagie roll. Here it goes over rice cooked in the same pan, which means all the sausage fat and pepper juice end up in the grain instead of soaking through bread. Each serving runs 620 calories with \u003cstrong\u003e26 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$2.30\u003c/strong\u003e. A spoonful of pesto stirred in at the end does more for it than any amount of extra seasoning.",
